          "amendment_id": "fr-4-5977fa01",
          "source_stage": "final_review",
          "source_cycle": 2,
          "source_completion_round": 4,
          "body": "The new alkalinity budget overloads a public mg-based API with meq values. `BudgetDelta::alkalinity` is stored in `ElementBudget { in_mg, out_mg }` ([crates/tank_core/src/types/budget.rs:34], [crates/tank_core/src/types/budget.rs:68]), and `SystemElementDelta` exposes the same `*_mg` fields for `Element::Alkalinity` ([crates/tank_core/src/budget_helpers.rs:64], [crates/tank_core/src/budget_helpers.rs:78]). The mismatch is already observable in the helper output: `assert_budget_balanced` and `assert_per_tick_balanced` still print `mg` for alkalinity entries ([crates/tank_core/src/budget_helpers.rs:472], [crates/tank_core/src/budget_helpers.rs:494]). This silently breaks the meaning of the serialized/debug budget surface and makes alkalinity diagnostics unreliable for downstream consumers.",
